title: Add InherentContext for verification-time inherent data providers
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `CreateInherentDataProviders` can now receive an explicit `InherentContext` in Aura and BABE import paths.

    This distinguishes block production (`Proposing`) from block verification (`Verifying { header, post_hash }`), allowing verification-time CIDPs to reconstruct inherent data that depends on the block being checked, such as header digests. Existing `()`-based CIDPs need to update these import-path signatures when used with Aura or BABE verification.
crates:
- name: sp-inherents
  bump: minor
